So that was a great
summary of how

00:22:32.100 --> 00:22:34.590
you can measure the
data protection service

00:22:34.590 --> 00:22:37.880
and be able to have different
layers of protection

00:22:37.880 --> 00:22:38.790
in the enterprise.

00:22:38.790 --> 00:22:41.220
I think you did a good
job in highlighting

00:22:41.220 --> 00:22:44.580
in an [INAUDIBLE] API
example, where the credit card

00:22:44.580 --> 00:22:46.032
information needs
to be protected.

00:22:46.032 --> 00:22:48.240
Maybe that was something
which was a mistake or error

00:22:48.240 --> 00:22:49.950
but the developer
didn't really notice.

00:22:49.950 --> 00:22:52.050
So let's now bring it
back to the same employee

00:22:52.050 --> 00:22:53.378
example of here.

00:22:53.378 --> 00:22:55.170
In this case, what I'm
going to do out here

00:22:55.170 --> 00:23:00.455
